{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "assignee": null, "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "", "closed_at": null, "closed_by_session": "", "compacted_at": null, "compacted_at_commit": null, "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "18f17543066cb9c34b95c905f778bc5c062a7c1d6d49bca3c068015d2540be09", "created_at": "2026-03-09T13:13:30Z", "created_by": "Marco Rotili", "crystallizes": false, "defer_until": null, "description": "## Problem\n\nSpotter has no way to view or annotate project plans (epic beads). Engineers must use the `bd` CLI to browse epics and tasks across projects (aufgabenschmiede, spotter, control_panel, levio). There is no centralized view of planned work, no rich rendering of bead content (mermaid diagrams, acceptance criteria tables, ASCII designs), and no way to annotate plans for review workflows.\n\n## Solution\n\nAdd a \"Plans\" section to the Spotter navigation that queries Dolt databases directly via MyXQL to display epic beads per project. The list view shows project filter chips with epic counts and an epic table. The detail view renders bead descriptions with rich content (markdown sections, mermaid diagrams, ASCII art, GIVEN/WHEN/THEN acceptance criteria tables) and expandable child tasks. Users can annotate plan text, with annotations linked to bead IDs for spotter-review integration.\n\n### Architecture\n\n- **Data source**: Direct MySQL queries against per-project Dolt servers (4 pools: spotter:13953, aufgabenschmiede:14117, control_panel:13818, levio:13641)\n- **No SQLite sync**: No Bead Ash resources or Oban sync jobs \u2014 read directly from Dolt\n- **Content parsing**: `BeadContentParser` extracts structured sections from markdown descriptions on read\n- **Annotation extension**: Existing `Annotation` Ash resource extended with `:plan` source type and `bead_id` string field\n- **Frontend**: Two LiveViews (PlansLive list, PlanDetailLive detail) with AshComputer pattern, new JS hooks for mermaid and block markdown\n- **New dependency**: mermaid.js (lazy-loaded via dynamic import)\n\n### Dolt Integration\n\nEach project runs its own Dolt server on a unique port. Key tables: `issues` (55 cols, VARCHAR PK), `dependencies` (composite PK), `comments`, `labels`. Dolt provides time-travel (`AS OF`), diffs (`dolt_diff`), and commit history (`dolt_log`) via SQL.\n\n## Data Model\n\n```mermaid\nerDiagram\n    DoltServer ||--o{ Issue : contains\n    Issue ||--o{ Dependency : has\n    Issue ||--o{ Comment : has\n    Issue ||--o{ Label : has\n    Project ||--o{ DoltServer : connects_to\n    Annotation }o--|| Issue : references_via_bead_id\n\n    DoltServer {\n        string host\n        int port\n        string database_name\n        string project_name\n    }\n    Issue {\n        string id PK\n        string title\n        text description\n        string status\n        int priority\n        string issue_type\n        string assignee\n        datetime created_at\n    }\n    Dependency {\n        string issue_id FK\n        string depends_on_id FK\n        string type\n    }\n    Annotation {\n        uuid id PK\n        atom source\n        string bead_id FK\n        string selected_text\n        string comment\n    }\n```\n\n## Product Skill Delta\n\n**Before**: No Plans feature. Bead data only accessible via `bd` CLI.\n\n**After**:\n- SKILL.md Feature Index: add `| Plans | /plans | plans.md |`\n- New `references/features/plans.md`: centralized view of project planning beads, rich rendering, annotations\n- `references/data-model.md`: Annotation extended with `bead_id` attribute and `plan` source value\n- `references/known-limitations.md`: Plans requires Dolt servers running; read-only; no real-time updates\n- `references/external-integrations.md`: `| Dolt (beads) | Epic/task bead data | MyXQL direct queries | Per-project Dolt server |`\n\n## Acceptance Tests\n\n- GIVEN Spotter is running WHEN the user views any page THEN a \"Plans\" link appears in the sidebar navigation\n- GIVEN projects exist in Spotter with Dolt servers running WHEN the user navigates to /plans THEN project filter chips are shown with epic counts from each Dolt database\n- GIVEN aufgabenschmiede has 3 epic beads WHEN the user clicks the aufgabenschmiede chip THEN all 3 epics are listed showing title, status badge, priority, child task count\n- GIVEN a project has zero epic beads WHEN the user selects that project chip THEN an empty state message is shown\n- GIVEN an epic bead with markdown description containing ## Problem, ## Solution, ## Acceptance Tests sections WHEN the user clicks that epic in the list THEN the detail view shows full description with rendered markdown\n- GIVEN an epic description contains a ```mermaid code block WHEN the detail view renders THEN the mermaid diagram is rendered as SVG\n- GIVEN an epic description has GIVEN/WHEN/THEN acceptance tests WHEN the detail view renders THEN acceptance tests are normalized into a structured table\n- GIVEN an epic has 4 child task beads WHEN the user views the epic detail THEN all 4 child tasks are listed below with id, title, status, priority\n- GIVEN a child task has its own description WHEN the user expands the task THEN the task description is rendered with the same rich rendering\n- GIVEN the user is viewing a plan detail WHEN they select text and create an annotation THEN an Annotation is created with source=plan and bead_id set\n- GIVEN plan annotations exist WHEN the user navigates to /reviews THEN plan annotations appear with \"Plan\" source badge\n- GIVEN plan annotations exist with bead_id WHEN spotter-review MCP queries annotations THEN plan annotations are included with bead_id\n- GIVEN the e2e test suite runs WHEN tests exercise the Plans section THEN fixtures use real bead data from Dolt\n- GIVEN Spotter is running with fixtures WHEN Playwright tests navigate to /plans and click an epic THEN list and detail views are verified with image snapshots\n\n## Rabbit Holes\n\n- Do not build a bead editor \u2014 Plans is read-only; bead creation/editing stays in bd CLI\n- Do not build real-time bead updates \u2014 no PubSub for Dolt changes; page refresh is fine\n- Do not parse all 55 bead columns \u2014 only parse what is needed for display\n- Do not build cross-project dependency graphs \u2014 show dependencies within an epic only\n- Do not build custom mermaid themes \u2014 use mermaid.js dark theme defaults\n- Do not attempt Ecto adapter for Dolt \u2014 use raw MyXQL queries for simplicity\n\n## No-gos\n\n- No bead write operations from Spotter (no create, update, close beads)\n- No authentication or access control on plans (localhost prototype)\n- No inline editing of acceptance criteria tables\n- No plan diffing or version history UI (future cycle \u2014 Dolt supports it via AS OF)\n- No WorksheetComposer or cross-project analytics\n\n## Classification\n\n- Type: feature\n- Architecture Change: additive (new LiveViews, new service modules, annotation extension)\n- Boundary Operation: read-only cross-system (Dolt MySQL queries)\n- Affected Boundaries: Spotter web layer, annotation system, frontend assets\n- Checkpoint Required: after Dolt client + annotation extension (tasks 1+3)\n\n---\nRig: spotter. Appetite: reviewed. Target: lib/spotter/beads/, lib/spotter_web/live/, lib/spotter_web/components/, assets/js/. Architecture: MyXQL direct Dolt queries + LiveView + annotation extension. Sources: .beads/dolt/config.yaml, lib/spotter/transcripts/annotation.ex, lib/spotter_web/components/layouts/root.html.heex, lib/spotter_web/router.ex, assets/js/app.js.", "design": "", "due_at": null, "ephemeral": false, "estimated_minutes": null, "event_kind": "", "external_ref": null, "hook_bead": "", "id": "spotter-3oj", "is_template": false, "issue_type": "epic", "last_activity": null, "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "original_size": null, "owner": "marco.rotili@handgemacht.ai", "payload": "", "pinned": false, "priority": 1, "quality_score": null, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "open", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Plans Navigation \u2014 View & Annotate Project Epics via Dolt", "updated_at": "2026-03-09T13:13:30Z", "waiters": [], "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
